WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.970
Smartphones have always posed challenges for parents of teens.
智能手机一直给青少年的父母带来挑战。

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:11.530
From social media apps to excessive screen time, the digital world is as threatening as the physical.
从社交媒体应用到过长的屏幕使用时间，数字世界和现实世界一样充满威胁。

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:19.750
A new study shows that about half of parents of teens are worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online.
一项新研究显示，在青少年的父母中，约有一半担心孩子在网上接触到露骨内容。

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.480
This is a valid concern, of course.
当然，这是一种合理的担忧。

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:32.230
But there are ways to alleviate the spread of explicit content, from changing the settings in their kids’ phones to monitoring such content with apps like Bark.
但有一些办法可以减少露骨内容的传播，从更改孩子手机上的设置，到用Bark之类的应用监控这类内容，不一而足。

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:41.310
Just as alarming, if not more so, is that the amount of time teens spend on social media can lead to anxiety and depression.
同样令人忧虑、甚至有过之而无不及的是，青少年花在社交媒体上的时长可能导致焦虑和抑郁。

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.840
Excessive screen time has detrimental effects, for a lot of obvious reasons.
过长的屏幕使用时间会造成有害影响，原因有很多，而且显而易见。

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:57.230
Constant media consumption inhibits healthy activities associated with childhood, like spending time outside, exercising, talking to friends and family.
不停地消费媒体内容会妨碍与童年相关的健康活动，比如待在户外、锻炼身体、和朋友家人聊天。

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.050
If it interferes with sleep, that’s even worse.
如果干扰到睡眠，那就更糟了。

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:09.530
Ample research shows too much smartphone use produces significant anxiety, depression, and feelings of isolation in teens.
大量研究表明，过度使用智能手机会让青少年产生严重的焦虑、抑郁和孤立感。

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:18.160
Teens log on to social media or spend time online trying to make connections, but end up feeling more alone and sadder than ever.
青少年登录社交媒体或花时间上网，想与人建立联系，最后却感到比以往任何时候都更孤单、更难过。

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:29.340
Faceless communication not only produces feelings of isolation and loneliness but increases instances of online bullying and susceptibility to criminal conduct.
不见面的交流不仅会让人产生孤立感和孤独感，还会增加网络欺凌事件，并使人更容易受到犯罪行为的影响。

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.210
Though I’ve banned most social media, I’ve still battled smartphone time with my own kids.
虽然我已经禁止自己的孩子使用大部分社交媒体，但还是一直在为智能手机使用时间和他们较劲。

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:40.690
A lot of the time I wish I could throw my kids’ smartphones into the nearest lake.
很多时候，我真希望能把孩子们的智能手机扔进最近的湖里。

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:58.180
The convenience of communication—when they need a ride home from school after practice, for instance—often feels like it isn’t worth the battle to keep their screen time low and productive, and continue to encourage “real-life” activities outside and with friends and family.
通讯上的便利——比如孩子训练结束后需要有人从学校接他们回家的时候——常常让人觉得抵不上这番较劲：既要让孩子的屏幕使用时间少而有益，又要继续鼓励他们在户外、和朋友家人一起参加“现实生活”中的活动。

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:05.400
I understand the addiction and often tell them I’m not sure how I would have handled having a smartphone as a teen.
我理解这种瘾，还常常跟他们说，要是我十几岁时有智能手机，我不确定自己会怎么应对。

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.950
As an adult, I, too, struggle with overuse.
作为成年人，我自己也苦于过度使用手机。

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:23.560
In a recent TV interview to promote a new film about a mother and daughter navigating social media use, actress Kate Winslet expressed her view on teens and social media—and her concern mirrors the trends.
女演员凯特·温斯莱特最近为宣传一部新电影接受了电视采访，影片讲述一对母女如何应对社交媒体使用问题；她在采访中表达了自己对青少年与社交媒体的看法，而她的担忧反映了上述趋势。

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:31.260
“I do definitely feel that the world of social media is frightening to parents because we don’t really know what’s there,” she said.
“我确确实实地感到，社交媒体的世界令父母害怕，因为我们并不真正知道那里面有什么。”她说。

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.310
“We don’t know how our children are using it.
“我们不知道孩子们是怎么使用它的。

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.850
We don’t know the effects that it’s really having on them.”
我们不知道它究竟在对孩子们产生什么影响。”

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:47.920
I don’t think the US government should regulate social media and teen smartphone use, but it is a vital topic for parents to understand and take seriously.
我不认为美国政府应该监管社交媒体和青少年使用智能手机的行为，但这是一个至关重要的话题，父母需要了解并认真对待。

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:59.500
Unfortunately, now, parents don’t just have to worry about real-world dangers, but also about all the ones sneaking online and the effects they have on teenagers and their mental health.
遗憾的是，如今父母不仅要担心现实世界中的危险，还要担心在网上悄然出没的所有危险，以及这些危险对青少年及其心理健康造成的影响。
